# AICL Example: Recommendation Engine
# Production recommendation system implementing collaborative filtering, content-based filtering,
# hybrid approach, cold start handling, A/B testing, and real-time update capabilities.

Goal Build a scalable recommendation engine that delivers personalized content recommendations using hybrid filtering approaches with sub-100ms latency, handles cold-start scenarios gracefully, and continuously improves through A/B testing and real-time feedback integration

Constraint Recommendation results must be generated within 100ms p99 latency for real-time serving paths
Constraint All recommendation logic must be auditable; must be able to explain why any recommendation was made
Constraint User data must never be used across tenants without explicit consent and isolation
Constraint Cold-start recommendations must maintain minimum 15% click-through rate
Constraint A/B test assignments must be deterministic per user and persist for test duration

Risk Collaborative filter echo chamber reinforcing narrow user profiles
Recovery Inject diversity-promoting items using exploration factor; apply inter-topic diversity penalties; monitor and cap content similarity within recommendation sets

Risk Cold-start failure for new users with no interaction history
Recovery Deploy popularity-based fallback with demographic segmentation; use onboarding survey to seed initial preferences; leverage item content features for content-based bootstrapping

Risk Real-time feature store lag causing stale user embeddings
Recovery Implement eventual consistency with read-repair pattern; serve from local cache with periodic refresh; fall back to last-known-good embedding on timeout

Risk A/B test contamination from cross-group assignment leakage
Recovery Use deterministic hash-based assignment with user ID salt; validate assignment consistency on every request; detect and quarantine misassigned users

Risk Model serving OOM during traffic spikes from large user embedding tables
Recovery Implement embedding table sharding across serving nodes; apply LRU eviction for cold embeddings; enable dynamic memory scaling with circuit breaker pattern

Risk Feedback loop from biased training data amplifying popularity bias
Recovery Apply inverse-propensity scoring to training weights; enforce exposure-adjusted ranking loss; periodically retrain from debiased data snapshot

Layer RecommendationServing
    SubLayer: RealTimeAPI
    SubLayer: BatchInference
    SubLayer: FeatureRetrieval
Layer ModelTraining
    SubLayer: CollaborativeFiltering
    SubLayer: ContentBasedFiltering
    SubLayer: HybridEnsemble
    SubLayer: ColdStartHandler
Layer Experimentation
    SubLayer: ABTestingFramework
    SubLayer: MetricCollection
    SubLayer: StatisticalAnalysis

Validation Recommendation latency must be below 100ms p99 under 10K QPS load
Validation Cold-start CTR must exceed 15% baseline within first 10 recommendations
Validation Diversity score (ILS) must remain above 0.4 for any recommendation set
Validation A/B test sample ratio must not deviate more than 1% from target allocation
Validation Embedding dimension consistency must be verified between training and serving
Validation Candidate generation must return at least 500 items before re-ranking stage
Validation Coverage metric must exceed 60% of catalog in recommendations over 24-hour window

# Level 2 - Entities

Entity UserProfile
    userId: string
    demographicInfo: dict
    interactionHistory: list
    embeddingVector: list
    preferenceVector: dict
    lastActiveTimestamp: datetime
    coldStartFlag: boolean
    tenantId: string
    consentFlags: dict

Entity ItemCatalog
    itemId: string
    itemType: string
    contentFeatures: dict
    embeddingVector: list
    popularityScore: float
    categoryPath: list
    createdAt: datetime
    activeStatus: boolean
    metadata: dict

Entity InteractionEvent
    eventId: string
    userId: string
    itemId: string
    eventType: string
    eventTimestamp: datetime
    dwellTimeSeconds: float
    contextFeatures: dict
    sessionId: string
    deviceType: string
    recommendationSource: string

Entity RecommendationSet
    requestId: string
    userId: string
    candidateItems: list
    rankedItems: list
    scores: dict
    explanations: dict
    diversityScore: float
    freshnessScore: float
    generatedAt: datetime
    modelVersion: string
    abTestGroup: string

Entity ABExperiment
    experimentId: string
    experimentName: string
    hypothesis: string
    controlVariant: dict
    treatmentVariants: list
    targetMetric: string
    sampleSizePerVariant: integer
    startDate: datetime
    endDate: datetime
    status: string
    statisticalPower: float

Entity ModelMetrics
    metricId: string
    modelVersion: string
    ndcgAtK: dict
    precisionAtK: dict
    recallAtK: dict
    mapScore: float
    coverageRatio: float
    diversityIndex: float
    noveltyScore: float
    fairnessScore: dict
    measuredAt: datetime

# Level 3 - Behaviors

Behavior GenerateCollaborativeRecommendations
    Input:
        userId: string
        candidatePoolSize: integer
    Output:
        candidateItems: list
        scores: dict
    Action:
        Retrieve user embedding vector from feature store
        Compute approximate nearest neighbor search in item embedding space
        Score candidates using dot product of user and item embeddings
        Apply popularity decay factor to reduce recency bias
        Return top candidatePoolSize items with scores

Behavior GenerateContentRecommendations
    Input:
        userId: string
        userInteractions: list
        candidatePoolSize: integer
    Output:
        candidateItems: list
        scores: dict
    Action:
        Extract content feature preferences from recent user interactions
        Build user content preference vector from liked item features
        Compute cosine similarity against item content feature matrix
        Boost novel items outside recent interaction neighborhoods
        Return top candidatePoolSize items with similarity scores

Behavior HybridRankRecommendations
    Input:
        collaborativeCandidates: list
        contentCandidates: list
        userProfile: UserProfile
    Output:
        finalRecommendations: RecommendationSet
    Action:
        Merge candidate sets with deduplication
        Compute hybrid score as weighted ensemble of collaborative and content scores
        Apply diversity penalty for intra-list similarity
        Apply freshness boost for recently added items
        Generate natural language explanations for top recommendations
        Compute diversity and coverage metrics for the final set
        Return ranked recommendation set

Behavior HandleColdStart
    Input:
        userId: string
        availableSignals: dict
    Output:
        coldStartRecommendations: RecommendationSet
        confidenceScore: float
    Action:
        Check if onboarding survey data is available
        If survey exists, map responses to preference vector
        If no survey, use demographic-based popularity ranking
        Apply exploration multiplier to increase diversity
        Set coldStartFlag on recommendation set
        Tag recommendations with low confidence score
        Emit ColdStartServed event for monitoring

Behavior ProcessInteractionFeedback
    Input:
        interactionEvent: InteractionEvent
    Output:
        updateAcknowledged: boolean
        embeddingDelta: dict
    Action:
        Validate interaction event schema and timestamp
        Update user interaction history in real-time store
        Compute incremental embedding update using online learning step
        Propagate embedding delta to feature store with versioning
        Update AB test metric counters for the assigned experiment
        Emit FeedbackProcessed event

Behavior RunABTestAnalysis
    Input:
        experimentId: string
        analysisDate: datetime
    Output:
        analysisReport: dict
        significanceResult: dict
    Action:
        Collect metric data for all experiment variants
        Compute sample statistics and effect sizes
        Run statistical significance test with multiple comparison correction
        Check for sample ratio mismatch across variants
        Generate recommendation on whether to ship treatment
        Emit ABTestResultReady event

# Level 4 - Conditions

Condition: ColdStartUserDetected
    When user has fewer than 5 interaction events in history
    Then route to HandleColdStart behavior; apply exploration-weighted recommendation strategy; log cold-start event for analysis

Condition: EmbeddingStalenessDetected
    When user embedding has not been updated in over 4 hours despite active sessions
    Then trigger priority embedding recomputation; serve from last-known-good embedding with staleness warning; alert feature pipeline

Condition: ABTestSignificanceReached
    When statistical test reaches p-value below 0.05 with adequate power
    Then auto-complete experiment; generate ship recommendation report; notify experiment owner and product team

Condition: RecommendationDiversityBelowThreshold
    When intra-list similarity exceeds 0.7 diversity threshold
    Then increase diversity penalty weight; inject exploration items from underrepresented categories; log diversity intervention

Condition: TrafficSpikeDetected
    When request rate exceeds 150% of baseline for 5 consecutive minutes
    Then activate pre-computed recommendation cache; reduce candidate pool size temporarily; scale serving replicas automatically

# Level 5 - Events

Event: ColdStartServed
    On cold-start recommendation generated for new user
    Action: track cold-start conversion metrics; trigger onboarding survey prompt; seed user profile with implicit signals

Event: FeedbackProcessed
    On interaction event successfully integrated into user model
    Action: update real-time feature store; increment AB test counters; refresh user embedding if delta exceeds threshold

Event: ABTestResultReady
    On statistical analysis of experiment completed
    Action: publish analysis report to experiment dashboard; notify stakeholders; schedule model promotion if treatment wins

Event: ModelRetrained
    On recommendation model retrained with new data
    Action: validate metrics against baseline; deploy to shadow serving; schedule canary rollout; update model registry

Event: EmbeddingUpdateRequired
    On detected staleness or feature drift in user/item embeddings
    Action: enqueue batch re-embedding job; prioritize active users; invalidate serving cache for affected entities

# Level 6 - Concurrency

Parallel:
    Collaborative and content-based candidate generation simultaneously
    Real-time embedding updates for multiple users
    AB test metric aggregation across variants
    Feature retrieval from online and offline stores
    Recommendation generation across multiple tenant partitions
    Embedding table compaction and serving simultaneously

# Level 7 - Optimization

Optimize: Recommendation relevance and user engagement
    Priority: Maximize NDCG@10 and CTR; balance relevance with diversity; minimize position bias in training data

Optimize: Real-time serving latency
    Priority: Sub-100ms p99 latency; pre-compute top-K for active users; use approximate nearest neighbor search with HNSW index

Optimize: Feature store query efficiency
    Priority: Cache hot user embeddings in local memory; batch embedding lookups; use columnar storage for feature retrieval

# Level 8 - Learning

Learn: Optimal hybrid ensemble weights
    Goal: Maximize recommendation quality combining collaborative and content signals
    Adapt: Ensemble weight parameters per user segment
    Based: Online bandit feedback from click-through and engagement signals

Learn: Cold-start strategy effectiveness
    Goal: Minimize time-to-effective-recommendations for new users
    Adapt: Cold-start exploration multiplier and fallback strategy selection
    Based: Cold-start conversion funnels and onboarding completion rates

Learn: Diversity vs relevance trade-off
    Goal: Find optimal diversity penalty that maximizes long-term engagement
    Adapt: Intra-list similarity penalty weight and exploration factor
    Based: Session-level engagement metrics and long-term retention curves

Learn: Feature importance for content filtering
    Goal: Identify most predictive content features for recommendation quality
    Adapt: Feature weight vector in content similarity computation
    Based: A/B test outcomes comparing feature weighting strategies

# Level 9 - Security

Security:
    Encrypt: User interaction history and preference vectors at rest using AES-256-GCM
    Encrypt: All API communication with TLS 1.3 and certificate pinning
    Protect: User PII with differential privacy noise injection before model training
    Protect: Tenant data isolation via logical partitioning with encryption per-tenant key
    Protect: AB test assignment integrity via signed experiment configuration
    Protect: Model serving endpoints with OAuth2 Bearer token authentication and rate limiting
    Encrypt: Embedding vectors in transit between training and serving infrastructure

# Level 10 - Native

Native: python
{
import numpy as np
from typing import Dict, List, Optional, Tuple
from dataclasses import dataclass, field
from collections import defaultdict

@dataclass
class HybridRecommender:
    collaborative_weight: float = 0.6
    content_weight: float = 0.4
    diversity_penalty: float = 0.3
    freshness_boost: float = 0.1
    exploration_factor: float = 0.15

    def rank_candidates(
        self,
        collab_scores: Dict[str, float],
        content_scores: Dict[str, float],
        item_features: Dict[str, np.ndarray],
        recent_items: List[str],
        top_k: int = 20
    ) -> List[Tuple[str, float]]:
        all_items = set(collab_scores.keys()) | set(content_scores.keys())
        scored_items = []

        for item_id in all_items:
            c_score = collab_scores.get(item_id, 0.0)
            ct_score = content_scores.get(item_id, 0.0)
            hybrid = (self.collaborative_weight * c_score +
                      self.content_weight * ct_score)
            scored_items.append((item_id, hybrid))

        scored_items.sort(key=lambda x: x[1], reverse=True)
        selected = []
        selected_features = []

        for item_id, score in scored_items:
            if len(selected) >= top_k:
                break
            feat = item_features.get(item_id, np.array([]))
            if len(selected_features) > 0 and len(feat) > 0:
                similarities = [
                    np.dot(feat, sf) / (np.linalg.norm(feat) * np.linalg.norm(sf) + 1e-8)
                    for sf in selected_features
                ]
                max_sim = max(similarities)
                score -= self.diversity_penalty * max_sim

            novelty_bonus = self.exploration_factor if item_id not in recent_items else 0.0
            score += novelty_bonus
            selected.append((item_id, score))
            if len(feat) > 0:
                selected_features.append(feat)

        selected.sort(key=lambda x: x[1], reverse=True)
        return selected

    def compute_diversity(self, items: List[str], features: Dict[str, np.ndarray]) -> float:
        if len(items) < 2:
            return 1.0
        embeddings = [features[i] for i in items if i in features]
        if len(embeddings) < 2:
            return 1.0
        total_sim = 0.0
        count = 0
        for i in range(len(embeddings)):
            for j in range(i + 1, len(embeddings)):
                sim = np.dot(embeddings[i], embeddings[j]) / (
                    np.linalg.norm(embeddings[i]) * np.linalg.norm(embeddings[j]) + 1e-8
                )
                total_sim += sim
                count += 1
        avg_sim = total_sim / count if count > 0 else 0
        return 1.0 - avg_sim

@dataclass
class ColdStartHandler:
    popularity_ranking: List[Tuple[str, float]] = field(default_factory=list)
    demographic_models: Dict[str, List[Tuple[str, float]]] = field(default_factory=dict)

    def recommend(self, user_signals: Dict, top_k: int = 20) -> List[Tuple[str, float]]:
        if "demographic_segment" in user_signals:
            segment = user_signals["demographic_segment"]
            if segment in self.demographic_models:
                return self.demographic_models[segment][:top_k]
        return self.popularity_ranking[:top_k]
}
